{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reduce high-dimensional feature spaces, uncover latent structures, and visualize complex datasets using PCA, Randomized SVD, and t-SNE."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/DimensionalityReduction","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"SwiftCluster"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Dimensionality Reduction & Manifold Learning"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PreparedPCA","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PCA","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/RandomizedSVD","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/TSNE"],"title":"Dimensionality Reduction","anchor":"Dimensionality-Reduction"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/ClusteringAndOutliers","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/VectorStoreAndRAG","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/HNSWVectorSearch"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"High-dimensional datasets frequently suffer from the “curse of dimensionality”—excessive noise, collinearity, high memory footprints, and difficulty in visualization. "},{"code":"SwiftCluster","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides a suite of linear and non-linear dimensionality reduction algorithms optimized for Apple Silicon unified memory:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PCA"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Exact Principal Component Analysis using singular value decomposition (SVD) with automatic CPU and UMA GPU hardware routing."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/RandomizedSVD"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Ultra-fast approximate rank-$k$ matrix decomposition following the Halko et al. (2011) algorithm for massive datasets."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/TSNE","type":"reference"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Non-linear manifold learning minimizing Kullback-Leibler divergence for 2D and 3D cluster visualization."}]}]}]},{"syntax":"mermaid","code":["graph TD","    HighDim[High-Dimensional Feature Matrix X: N x D] --> Choice{Decomposition Strategy}","    Choice -->|Linear Global Variance| PCA[PCA: SVD Decomposition]","    Choice -->|Massive Dense Matrix| RSVD[RandomizedSVD: Low-Rank Projection]","    Choice -->|Non-Linear Cluster Visualization| TSNE[t-SNE: Manifold Probabilities]","    PCA --> LowDimLinear[Reduced Feature Matrix: N x k]","    RSVD --> Factors[Low-Rank Factors: U, S, Vt]","    TSNE --> Vis2D[2D\/3D Embedding Coordinates]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"1. Principal Component Analysis (PCA)","anchor":"1-Principal-Component-Analysis-PCA","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Principal Component Analysis finds orthogonal projection axes (principal components) that maximize the variance of the data.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Fitting and Transforming","anchor":"Fitting-and-Transforming","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftCluster","","\/\/ 1. Initialize PCA to extract 3 principal components","let pca = PCA(nComponents: 3, device: .auto)","","\/\/ 2. Fit and project the data matrix [N rows x D columns]","let X_reduced = try await pca.fitTransform(featureMatrix)","","\/\/ 3. Inspect explained variance ratios","if let ratios = pca.explainedVarianceRatio {","    print(\"Explained variance per component: \\(ratios)\")","    let cumulative = ratios.reduce(0.0, +)","    print(\"Total captured variance: \\(String(format: \"%.2f%%\", cumulative * 100))\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Choosing Optimal Components (Scree Analysis)","anchor":"Choosing-Optimal-Components-Scree-Analysis","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Analyze the cumulative variance to select the minimal number of components capturing $90%+$ of total data variance:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var cumulativeSum = 0.0","for (index, ratio) in (pca.explainedVarianceRatio ?? []).enumerated() {","    cumulativeSum += ratio","    print(\"PC\\(index + 1): \\(String(format: \"%.3f\", ratio)) | Cumulative: \\(String(format: \"%.1f%%\", cumulativeSum * 100))\")","    if cumulativeSum >= 0.90 {","        print(\">> Recommended cutoff: \\(index + 1) components\")","        break","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"2. Approximate Low-Rank SVD (`RandomizedSVD`)","anchor":"2-Approximate-Low-Rank-SVD-RandomizedSVD","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When factorizing massive matrices where $k \\ll \\min(M, N)$, standard deterministic LAPACK SVD ($O(MN^2)$) becomes memory- and compute-prohibitive. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/RandomizedSVD","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" computes an approximate rank-$k$ factorization $X \\approx U \\cdot \\text{diag}(S) \\cdot V^T$ in $O(MNk)$ using randomized sketching:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftCluster","","\/\/ Factorize a 10,000 x 500 matrix into top 20 singular components","let svdResult = try RandomizedSVD.compute(","    X: largeMatrix,","    nComponents: 20,","    nOversamples: 10,  \/\/ Oversampling p for stability","    nPowerIter: 2,     \/\/ Power iterations q for slow spectral decay","    seed: 42",")","","print(\"Left singular vectors U: [\\(svdResult.U.count) x \\(svdResult.U.first?.count ?? 0)]\")","print(\"Top singular values S: \\(svdResult.S.prefix(5))\")","print(\"Right singular vectors Vt: [\\(svdResult.Vt.count) x \\(svdResult.Vt.first?.count ?? 0)]\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"3. Non-Linear Visualization with t-SNE","anchor":"3-Non-Linear-Visualization-with-t-SNE","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"While PCA preserves global variance, t-Distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding (t-SNE) preserves local neighborhood similarities, making it ideal for visualizing non-linear clusters, high-dimensional embeddings, and classification manifolds in 2D or 3D.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftCluster","","\/\/ 1. Initialize t-SNE actor","let tsne = TSNE(","    nComponents: 2,","    perplexity: 30.0,","    learningRate: 200.0,","    maxIterations: 1000,","    seed: 42",")","","\/\/ 2. Perform non-linear embedding","let coordinates2D = try await tsne.fitTransform(featureMatrix)","","\/\/ 3. Inspect final optimization divergence","if let klLoss = await tsne.klDivergence {","    print(\"Final KL Divergence: \\(klLoss)\")","}","","\/\/ 4. Pass coordinates to SwiftVisualization for interactive scatter plots","for point in coordinates2D.prefix(5) {","    print(\"X: \\(point[0]), Y: \\(point[1])\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"4. Hardware Routing & Device Selection","anchor":"4-Hardware-Routing--Device-Selection","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PCA","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" accepts an ","type":"text"},{"code":"ExecutionDevice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PreparedPCA","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for numerical precision and ownership details.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Device mode","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Behavior","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".auto","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Uses the existing hardware router to choose a fitting device.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".cpu","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Uses Double Accelerate LAPACK or randomized SVD, according to the selected solver.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".gpu","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Uses Float MLX conversion and centering, then SVD on the CPU stream.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".ane","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Uses the existing router fallback for unsupported ANE execution.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"type":"thematicBreak"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/dimensionalityreduction"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster":{"abstract":[{"text":"PCA Dimensionality Reduction & Unsupervised Clustering.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiftCluster","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/ClusteringAndOutliers":{"abstract":[{"text":"High-performance clustering and density-based anomaly detection powered by ","type":"text"},{"code":"KDTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DBSCAN","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"KMeans","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"LocalOutlierFactor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"IsolationForest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Spatial Indexing, Clustering & Outlier Detection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/ClusteringAndOutliers","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/clusteringandoutliers"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/TSNE":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TSNE"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/tsne","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TSNE","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"TSNE","abstract":[{"text":"t-Distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding (t-SNE) for non-linear dimensionality reduction and manifold learning.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/TSNE","role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/PreparedPCA":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Fit preprocessing on training observations, apply the fitted preprocessing to held-out observations, and pass prepared data directly to PCA. PCA returns component scores with feature names and original row positions.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","title":"Fit and project prepared data with PCA","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/preparedpca","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PreparedPCA","role":"article"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/RandomizedSVD":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RandomizedSVD"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/randomizedsvd","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RandomizedSVD"}],"type":"topic","title":"RandomizedSVD","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Randomized Singular Value Decomposition using the Halko et al. (2011) algorithm."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/RandomizedSVD","role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/PCA":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PCA"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/pca","abstract":[{"text":"Principal component analysis with explicit CPU solver and device choices.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Prepared inputs retain feature identity and return named, provenance-preserving scores.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PCA","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PCA"}],"type":"topic","title":"PCA"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/HNSWVectorSearch":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/HNSWVectorSearch","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Scale approximate nearest neighbor (ANN) retrieval logarithmically using Hierarchical Navigable Small World graphs."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/hnswvectorsearch","role":"collectionGroup","title":"High-Dimensional Vector Search with HNSW"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/VectorStoreAndRAG":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/vectorstoreandrag","type":"topic","title":"In-Memory VectorStore & On-Device RAG","abstract":[{"text":"Build low-latency semantic search, embedding retrieval, and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines on Apple Silicon using SIMD Accelerate.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/VectorStoreAndRAG","role":"collectionGroup"}}}